  "name": {
    "en": "Introduction to Machine Learning Part 1: Foundations"
  },
  "description": [
    {
      "type": "TextObject",
      "inLanguage": "en",
      "text": "\u003Ch5\u003E\u003Cspan style=\"\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"\" style=\"font-weight: normal; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"\u003E\r\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EMachine Learning (ML)&nbsp;\u003C/strong\u003Eis at the core of many applications of \u003Cstrong\u003Eartificial intelligence\u003C/strong\u003E. A key goal of this course series is to teach the \u003Cstrong\u003Efundamental building blocks \u003C/strong\u003Ebehind\u003Cstrong\u003E supervised ML\u003C/strong\u003E. Additional to \u003Cstrong\u003Eunderstanding\u003C/strong\u003E the theoretical basics, participants will learn how to \u003Cstrong\u003Eapply\u003C/strong\u003E and evaluate different ML algorithms in \u003Cstrong\u003ER and Python \u003C/strong\u003Ewith a focus on tabular data.\u003C/p\u003E\r\n\u003Cp\u003EAfter a general \u003Cstrong\u003Eintroduction to the basics of ML\u003C/strong\u003E in part 1/3, participants will get in touch with several \u003Cstrong\u003Elearning algorithms\u003C/strong\u003E&nbsp;in part 2/3. Finally, we will cover the \u003Cstrong\u003Eevaluation and tuning of ML models\u003C/strong\u003E in depth in part 3/3.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/h5\u003E",
      "encodingFormat": "text/html"
    }
